{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ROM",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore being justified by faith, we have peace with God, through our Lord Jesus Christ:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By whom also we have access by faith into this grace in which we stand, and rejoice in hope of the glory of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And not only ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", but we glory in tribulations also; knowing that tribulation worketh patience;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And patience, experience; and experience, hope:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And hope maketh not ashamed, because the love of God is shed abroad in our hearts, by the Holy Spirit which is given to us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For when we were yet without strength, in due time Christ died for the ungodly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For scarcely for a righteous man will one die: yet perhaps for a good man some would even dare to die.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But God commendeth his love towards us, in that while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Much more then, being now justified by his blood, we shall be saved from wrath through him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if when we were enemies, we were reconciled to God by the death of his Son; much more, being reconciled, we shall be saved by his life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And not only ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", but we also joy in God, through our Lord Jesus Christ, by whom we have now received the atonement.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For until the law, sin was in the world: but sin is not imputed when there is no law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless, death reigned from Adam to Moses, even over them that had not sinned after the similitude of Adam's transgression, who is the figure of him that was to come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But not as the offense, so also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the free gift. For if through the offense of one many are dead, much more the grace of God, and the gift by grace, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by one man, Jesus Christ, hath abounded to many.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And not as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by one that sinned, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the gift. For the judgment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by one to condemnation, but the free gift ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of many offenses to justification.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if by one man's offense death reigned by one; much more they who receive abundance of grace, and of the gift of righteousness, shall reign in life by one, Jesus Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore, as by the offense of one, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "judgment came",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon all men to condemnation, even so by the righteousness of one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the free gift came",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon all men to justification of life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For as by one man's disobedience many were made sinners, so by the obedience of one shall many be made righteous.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover the law entered, that the offense might abound. But where sin abounded, grace did much more abound:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.5.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.5.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That as sin hath reigned to death, even so might grace reign through righteousness to eternal life, by Jesus Christ our Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
